{"name":"Solarium","hex":"#e1ba36","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Solarium","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A large monument in ancient Rome and its modern ruins.","A former constellation located between the constellations of Horologium, Dorado, and Hydrus"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Solarium"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sunroom","blocks":[{"text":"A sunroom, also frequently called a solarium, is a room that permits abundant daylight and views of the landscape while sheltering from adverse weather. Sunroom and solarium have the same denotation: solarium is Latin for \"place of sun[light]\". Solaria of various forms have been erected throughout European history. Currently, the sunroom or solarium is popular in Europe, Canada, the United States, Australia, and New Zealand. Sunrooms may feature passive solar building design to heat and illuminate them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Hatoyama_Hall_%28sun-room%29.jpg/330px-Hatoyama_Hall_%28sun-room%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunroom"},{"title":"Terrace (building)","blocks":[{"text":"A terrace is an external, raised, open, flat area in either a landscape near a building, or as a roof terrace on a flat roof."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Tree_on_UCLA_campus.jpg/330px-Tree_on_UCLA_campus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrace_(building)"},{"title":"Solarium (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Solarium is a 2021 French short film directed by Jonathan Koulavsky. The thirty-minute story follows a young driver of trot racing as he experiences self-doubt, frustration, and isolation. The short has been presented at a number of festivals, including the 2022 Rhode Island International Film Festival. The film is part of the 2023 César Narrative Short Films Selection."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/33/Solarium_Film_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solarium_(film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Wintergarten_%28Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz%29_%28Anemometer%29.jpg/500px-Wintergarten_%28Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz%29_%28Anemometer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Wintergarten_%28Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz%29_%28Anemometer%29.jpg/1280px-Wintergarten_%28Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz%29_%28Anemometer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Wintergarten_%28Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz%29_%28Anemometer%29.jpg/500px-Wintergarten_%28Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz%29_%28Anemometer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A German \"Wintergarten\" with open blinds and anemometer (top left)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWintergarten_(Eingefahrener_Sonnenschutz)_(Anemometer).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Jamnagar_Solarium_-_Indian_Review_1936_-_37-3.jpg/500px-Jamnagar_Solarium_-_Indian_Review_1936_-_37-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Jamnagar_Solarium_-_Indian_Review_1936_-_37-3.jpg/500px-Jamnagar_Solarium_-_Indian_Review_1936_-_37-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Revolving solarium in Jamnagar, India designed by Jean Saidman","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJamnagar_Solarium_-_Indian_Review_1936_-_37-3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Joenniem